            "review_title": "Review at Miss Hà Nội",
            "review_text": "Dream09814029678\n10 contributions\n0\nWhere Vietnam’s Soul Meets the Plate\nMay 2026 • Friends\nMiss Hà Nội is one of those rare places that makes you fall in love with Vietnamese food all over again. Tucked near the Temple of Literature, it's a modern folk snack bar with serious culinary intention — every dish name tells a story, the space has warmth and character, and the kitchen clearly knows what it's doing.\nThe mini bánh mì selection alone is worth the visit. The Bánh Mì Nhớ Mẹ — caramelised braised pork with fermented mustard greens — hits that perfect sweet-salty-tangy balance that takes you straight back to a home kitchen. The Bánh Mì Hàng Xóm (braised pork ear and tongue) is rustic, textured, and deeply satisfying.\nThis isn't tourist food dressed up in a nice room. It's Vietnamese food done with pride, creativity, and soul. Highly recommended for anyone who wants to eat real Hanoi — no Michelin star required.\nRead more\nWritten May 28, 2026",
